Charlie’s work rate is  

\[
\text{combined rate}= \frac{1}{3}\text{ job/hour}
\]

Alice’s rate = \( \frac{1}{6}\) job/hour, Bob’s rate = \( \frac{1}{12}\) job/hour.

\[
\text{Charlie’s rate}= \frac{1}{3} - \left(\frac{1}{6}+\frac{1}{12}\right)
= \frac{1}{3} - \frac{1}{4}
= \frac{4-3}{12}
= \frac{1}{12}\text{ job/hour}
\]

Thus Charlie would need \(12\) hours to complete the job alone.

Final answer: 12 hours.

